{
  "title": "Dirt Delay",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Two delays in series,",
        "each fed through",
        "drive or bitcrush.",
        "",
        "Grown from a Daisy",
        "Versio patch.",
        "",
        "The first echo comes",
        "back at twice Time:",
        "both delays share it.",
        "",
        "Stereo: the left",
        "side runs at 3/4",
        "of Time, so the",
        "echoes land apart.",
        "",
        "Mix changes the",
        "balance, never the",
        "volume."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Controls",
      "lines": [
        "1 Mix: dry / wet",
        "2 Drive: drive AND",
        "  downsample",
        "3 Time: 0-250 ms",
        "4 Fdbk: repeats",
        "5 Crush: bit depth",
        "6 Gain: input level",
        "  into the drive",
        "7 FX 1: Off/OD/BC",
        "8 FX 2: Off/OD/BC",
        "",
        "Everything is on",
        "one page."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Gain and Drive",
      "lines": [
        "Gain pushes the",
        "signal into the",
        "drive, up to +24 dB.",
        "For a Move track",
        "that is the hot",
        "level a Eurorack",
        "patch would send.",
        "",
        "Drive sets how hard",
        "it saturates, from",
        "0.3 (just warm) up.",
        "",
        "The wet volume stays",
        "put: turn either one",
        "and only the",
        "character changes.",
        "",
        "A fixed bass boost",
        "(+6 dB at 100 Hz)",
        "sits before the",
        "drive, so the low",
        "end is what gets",
        "pushed hardest."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "FX 1 and FX 2",
      "lines": [
        "The Versio's two",
        "switches.",
        "",
        "FX 1 sits before the",
        "first delay, FX 2",
        "between the two.",
        "",
        "Off: straight on",
        "OD: overdrive",
        "BC: bitcrush and",
        "    downsample",
        "",
        "Crush sets the bits,",
        "Drive sets the",
        "sample-rate drop.",
        "",
        "As on the Versio,",
        "FX 2's OD follows",
        "Drive only while",
        "FX 1 is on OD too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Level Match",
      "lines": [
        "Always on. The wet",
        "path is brought to",
        "the dry level, and",
        "the crossfade keeps",
        "power constant.",
        "",
        "It settles in about",
        "half a second. A",
        "sudden jump is held",
        "to +3 dB at once.",
        "",
        "A ringing tail is",
        "left alone to fade."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
